{"step_index":397,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-08T10:39:16Z","content":"The **Dockerfiles** and **Docker Compose configurations** have been created and hardened for your application:\n\n---\n\n### 📄 Created Docker Files & Configurations\n\n1. **Backend Multi-Stage Hardened Dockerfile**: [`backend/Dockerfile`](file:///c:/Users/addal/Documents/antigravity/focused-bell/backend/Dockerfile)\n   * Multi-stage build (`python:3.11-slim`).\n   * Unprivileged non-root user execution (`appuser`, UID `10001`).\n   * Exposes port `8001`.\n2. **Frontend Multi-Stage Hardened Dockerfile**: [`frontend/Dockerfile`](file:///c:/Users/addal/Documents/antigravity/focused-bell/frontend/Dockerfile)\n   * Multi-stage build (`node:20-alpine`).\n   * Non-root `appuser` (UID `10002`) serving static production builds via `serve`.\n3. **Orchestration Config**: [`docker-compose.yml`](file:///c:/Users/addal/Documents/antigravity/focused-bell/docker-compose.yml)\n\n---\n\n### 🛠️ How to Compile the Docker Images on Your Laptop\n\nI triggered **Docker Desktop** to launch on your machine. To compile the actual Docker image layers on your laptop:\n\n1. Look at your Windows Taskbar / System Tray and make sure **Docker Desktop** is open and shows **\"Docker Desktop is running\"** (green icon).\n2. Open PowerShell and run this command:\n   ```powershell\n   cd c:\\Users\\addal\\Documents\\antigravity\\focused-bell\n\n   docker-compose up --build\n   ```\n3. Docker will build both images (`securechain-backend:v1.0.0` and `securechain-frontend:v1.0.0`) and launch both containers!"}
